  "id": "Compound::DB00678 - Gene::5243",
  "verbalization": "Losartan is implicated in the pathogenesis of Abcb1 through a series of interconnected mechanisms involving cardiovascular and antihypertensive pathways. The evidence suggests that Losartan, through its role in causing conditions like Essential Hypertension and Coxalgia, indirectly influences Abcb1 expression or function. Both Essential Hypertension and Coxalgia are associated with Lisinopril, an antihypertensive agent that binds Abcb1, indicating a shared regulatory pathway. The lowest common ancestors of Losartan and Lisinopril, both belonging to the Organonitrogen Heterocyclic Compound class and the Antihypertensive Agent category, suggest a broader pharmacological context where these drugs interact with Abcb1. The cumulative evidence points to a potential mechanism where Losartan, via its effects on cardiovascular conditions, may modulate Abcb1 activity, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be elucidated.",
